RecRanger wrote:

> If an uncursed item is on top of any number of cursed items,
> doesn't the pet ignore the items under the uncursed object
> and move to that space?

No.

A single cursed item in a stack will prevent the pet from moving onto
that stack (except of course that there's still a small chance it will
do so, but "reluctantly").

I believe that when a pet moves onto a stack "reluctantly", it may pick
up an item from that stack, provided that this top item isn't cursed
itself.

So if a square contains a cursed item with an uncursed on top of it, a
pet will only move onto that square "reluctantly", but when it does so,
it may pick up the uncursed top item.

